# Obsidian and CodeMirror 6 Development Standards

## Context

- Apply when users are developing Obsidian plugins
- Apply when working with CodeMirror 6 editor related functionality
- Ensure code follows official documentation standards and best practices

## Critical Rules

### Obsidian Plugin Development Standards

- Strictly follow Obsidian API documentation (https://docs.obsidian.md/Home)
- Use TypeScript for all plugin components
- Plugin structure must include main.ts, manifest.json and styles.css (if needed)
- Use Obsidian's Plugin class as base class
- Implement onload() and onunload() lifecycle methods
- Use registerEvent() to register event listeners
- Use addCommand() to register commands
- Use addSettingTab() to add setting options
- Use Obsidian provided UI components (Modal, Notice etc.)
- Avoid direct DOM manipulation, use methods provided by Obsidian API

### CodeMirror 6 Development Standards

- Follow CodeMirror 6 official documentation (https://codemirror.net/docs/)
- Use core concepts like EditorState, EditorView and StateField
- Use Extension system to add functionality
- Manage state changes through StateEffect and Transaction
- Use Decoration to modify text display
- Consider performance impact when implementing extensions
- Use Facet to define configuration options
- Pay attention to event propagation and state synchronization when integrating CodeMirror with Obsidian editor
- Use ViewPlugin to implement view-related functionality
- Use WidgetType to create custom inline components

## Examples

<example>
// Valid Obsidian plugin initialization example
export default class MyPlugin extends Plugin {
  async onload() {
    console.log('Loading plugin');
    
    // Register command
    this.addCommand({
      id: 'sample-command',
      name: 'Example Command',
      callback: () => {
        new Notice('Command executed');
      }
    });

    // Register CodeMirror extension
    this.registerEditorExtension([
      Prec.highest(EditorView.domEventHandlers({
        click: (event, view) => {
          // Handle click event
          return false;
        }
      }))
    ]);
  }

  onunload() {
    console.log('Unloading plugin');
  }
}
</example>

<example type="invalid">
// Invalid implementation
class BadPlugin {
  constructor() {
    // Not extending Plugin class
    document.querySelector('.editor').addEventListener('click', this.onClick);
  }
  
  onClick() {
    // Direct DOM manipulation instead of using Obsidian API
    document.body.innerHTML += '<div>New content</div>';
  }
  
  // Missing required lifecycle methods
}

// Incorrect CodeMirror implementation
const wrongExtension = {
  // Not using proper Extension system
  init: function(editor) {
    editor.on('change', function() {
      // Using outdated API
    });
  }
};
</example> 